<title>FRANCE: U.S. main origin for Paris Jan-Apr 97 air imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. main origin for Paris Jan-Apr 97 air imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in January-April 1997, Paris airport authority, ADP, figures show.</p>
<p>In Jan-Apr import traffic to the Paris  airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 179,171 , an increase of 3.6 percent on the same period last year, Aeroports de Paris ADP, figures show. downendsdown</p>
<p>The main countries of origin for ADP imports in Jan-Apr with percentage change on Jan-Apr last year were:</p>
<p>  1. United States     48,358     down   3.2</p>
<p>  2. Japan		  8,676     up    51.6</p>
<p>  3. India		  8,617     down   7.4</p>
<p>  4. Canada		 7,516     down  18.8</p>
<p>  5. U.K.		   7,128     up    35.0</p>
<p>  6. Hong Kong	    6,496     up    11.8</p>
<p>  7. Germany		5,349     up    18.1</p>
<p>  8. Thailand	     4,529     up    38.5</p>
<p>  9. Fr.W Indies	  4,025     up     7.4</p>
<p> 10. Senegal		3,756     up    13.5</p>
<p> 11. Italy		  3,627     down   8.3</p>
<p> 12. Singapore	    3,167     up    80.1</p>
<p> 13. Kenya		  3,001     down  21.5</p>
<p> 14. Morocco		2,565     down  25.5</p>
<p> 15. Brazil		 2,403     up    29.7</p>
<p> 16. Argentine	    2,349     unchanged</p>
<p> 17. China		  2,251     up    60.9</p>
<p> 18. Egypt		  2,212     up    28.4</p>
<p> 19. Korea		  2,200     up    30.9</p>
<p> 20. Switzerland	  1,984     up    17.6</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Service Tel+ 44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017 - www.racs.com</p>
